    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nOne file, `SaveOwner.java` \u2014 the single natural place, since it already runs on successful create, computes `memberId` (the owner's `customerCode`), and has `owner.getId()` in hand:\n\n- Added a `NOTIFY` logger alongside the existing `AUDIT` one.\n- Added one line emitting the welcome notification:\n  ```java\n  NOTIFY.info(\"welcome ownerId={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), memberId);\n  ```\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\n`SaveOwner` has a single public method (`service`), so its `WMC_other` is 0 (\u2192 1) and the method is straight-line (CC = 1). Only that one simple function changed, in one file, with no new class or pipeline step \u2014 the cheapest option under the cost formula. Emitting inside `SaveOwner` reuses the already-computed `memberId` rather than recomputing the identity, so no new logic was introduced.\n\nThe new test `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes \u2014 the `NOTIFY` line carries both the owner id and the memberId (`NOTIFY - welcome ownerId=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`).",
